WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:04.698
First: why does the audit
read refuse a window

3
00:00:04.698 --> 00:00:07.587
that starts more than
thirty days before the run?

4
00:00:07.587 --> 00:00:13.109
The answer is b: Microsoft Entra audit logs
are kept for thirty days with P1 or P2,

5
00:00:13.109 --> 00:00:18.375
so older events can't be read, and the
window would look complete when it isn't.

6
00:00:18.375 --> 00:00:21.725
Second: what does the hash
chain between packages show?

7
00:00:21.725 --> 00:00:26.013
The answer is b: a replaced package
or a missing day, as a break,

8
00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:30.913
because each package records the
previous package's manifest hash.

9
00:00:30.913 --> 00:00:35.913
You saw the chain in Lab 1, step eight,
and an edited package fail in step ten.

10
00:00:35.913 --> 00:00:40.870
The module page has two more questions,
each linked to the section that answers it.
